===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=preposition|:der|la:per|tree=1}}
From {{der|en|la|per||through, during}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*per}}. {{doublet|en|par}}.

====Preposition====
{{en-head|prep}}

# For each.
#: {{ux|en|Admission is £10 '''per''' person.}}
#: {{ux|en|miles '''per''' gallon}}
#: {{ux|en|beats '''per''' minute}}
#: {{ux|en|$2.50 '''per''' dozen}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Thomas Schlacher|title=Joel Embiid vs. Nikola Jokić vs. Giannis Antetokounmpo: What’s the latest in the race to become the NBA MVP?|url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/04/05/sport/nba-mvp-race-jokic-embiid-giannis-spt-intl|date=2023-04-05|passage=The Nuggets star is averaging 24.9 PPG, 11.9 RPG (rebounds '''per''' game) and an agonizing 9.9 APG (assists '''per''' game) – demonstrating Jokić’s incredible all-around ability.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251008000249/https://www.cnn.com/2023/04/05/sport/nba-mvp-race-jokic-embiid-giannis-spt-intl|archivedate=8 October 2025}}
# To each, in each ({{non-gloss|used in expressing [[ratio]]s of [[unit]]s}}).
#: {{ux|en|12 inches '''per''' foot}}
#: {{ux|en|100 centimeters '''per''' meter}}
# {{lb|en|medicine}} By the, through the ({{non-gloss|with name of body part in Latin}}).
#: {{ux|en|Introduce the endoscope '''per''' nasum.}}
#: {{ux|en|The medication is to be administered '''per''' os.}}
# In accordance with, [[as per]].
#: {{ux|en|I parked my car at the curb '''per''' your request.}}
#: {{ux|en|Implement a program that computes the approximate grade level needed to comprehend some text, '''per''' the below.}}
#: {{ux|en|Note that while the walkthrough illustrates that words may be separated by more than one space, you may assume, '''per''' the specifications above, that no sentences will contain more than one space in a row.}}
# [[according to|According to]].
#: {{ux|en|Bucks trading for Patrick Beverley, '''per''' sources}}
#: {{ux|en|The Heat were too close to the luxury tax line -- $1.6 million over before this trade, '''per''' ESPN's Bobby Marks}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In senses equivalent to "each", ''per'' is typically followed by a singular noun phrase with no [[determiner]].
*: ''Take one pill '''per''' day,'' not ''*Take one pill '''per''' a day.''
* The common exception is its use with plural noun phrases, although these are almost always limited to large round numbers such as 100, 1,000, 10,000...
*: ''The abortion rate in the U.S. has dropped since 1980 from nearly 30 '''per''' 1,000 women of childbearing age to less than 20.''
* In medical senses, ''per'' is followed by the name of an orifice in Latin rather than English (for example, ''[[per os]]'', ''[[per rectum]]'', ''[[per vaginam]]''); in the postwar era there has been a continual shift toward preferring an English equivalent, especially but not solely when communicating with patients: ''by mouth'' or ''[[orally]]'', ''[[rectally]]'', ''[[vaginally]]'', etc. (More at Wikipedia at ''{{w|plain language}}''.)

